description: 'v031''s exact recipe with a BETTER TEACHER. Student unchanged: hidden
  128, input_proj 64, distill_weight 2.0, 3 epochs, same architecture and seed. Only
  the distillation targets change.'
hypothesis: "The teacher's quality is the one input to distillation we have never\
  \ varied, and a strictly better one is on disk. Our current teacher is dozken's\
  \ reset2k at 0.6864 local. His two-graph loss-diverse ensemble of reset2k + reset4k\
  \ is 0.6879, which is 0.0015 better, and it is free at inference because a teacher\
  \ never runs at serving time.\n\n  TeacherStore already averages multiple label\
  \ files on read, so pointing loss.teacher_labels at both members reproduces his\
  \ raw-mean ensemble exactly with no change to the training script. His solution.py\
  \ confirms the average is raw (scale = 1/len(graphs), no z-scoring), which matters\
  \ because the metric clips at +/-2.\n\n  The honest prior is POOR and stated as\
  \ such. dozken's distil_ens scored 0.6585 against his distil160's 0.6588, so on\
  \ his pair a better teacher did not beat a worse one through compression. The visible\
  \ reason is that his student already sat at the compression sweet spot, leaving\
  \ no gap for the teacher's extra 0.0015 to close.\n\n  Our student is somewhere\
  \ different: 225,922 params at 0.687376 against a 0.6864 teacher, so it has ALREADY\
  \ OVERTAKEN the single-model teacher. That is new -- none of dozken's students beat\
  \ their own teacher locally. Whether that means there is headroom for a better teacher,\
  \ or that the student has extracted everything extractable, is exactly the question.\
  \ Worth one run, not worth assuming."
change_vs_parent: loss.teacher_labels gains a second member so TeacherStore averages
  dozken's reset2k and reset4k into his 0.6879 ensemble. Student architecture, distill_weight,
  schedule and seed all unchanged.
